  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nSOFO Archive Galleries\n\nBelow is a library of our archive galleries. Each gallery contains images that you can purchase as high-resolution downloads for either personal or commercial use.\n\nOnce you have completed your purchase, you will be emailed with login details to download your images.\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum Education Collection: WW2 Evacuees\nImages of objects from the museum's education collection, used in handling sessions and educational resources\nWyld Atlas - Peninsular War Maps\nJames Wyld's Atlas with detailed maps of Peninsular War battles. c.1840\nWinston Churchill - Queens Own Oxfordshire Hussar\nImages related to Winston Churchill' service with the Queens Own Oxfordshire Hussars (Oxfordshire Yeomanry). Pre-1914.\nCassel 1940\nPhotographs taken in and around Cassel, 1940 [4th (Territorial) Battalion, Oxfordshire & Buckinghamshire Light Infantry]\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
